<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion. See NDA__c.Move_to_Signed
         .quickAction-meta.xml for the full rationale behind this set of per-hop actions (user
         decision, 2026-08-26) and for why no <description> element is used.
         ⚠ NDA__c.Move_to_Approved.quickAction-meta.xml, previously cross-referenced here, was
         DELETED 2026-08-31 (Tranche 3, item 2d/D-7) - it was the one-click Prepare -> Approved
         bypass of the new NDA_Issue_Approval process; see that approval file's own comment and
         flexipages/NDA_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml's for the retirement argument.

         THE 'Sent' HOP. NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps BOTH 'Approved' => 'Sent' AND the legacy
         'Not Sent' => 'Sent', so this ONE action is placed on NDA_Record_Page TWICE, as two
         valueListItems carrying the same <value> and different stage criteria.

         🔴 THAT IS THE DUPLICATE-ENTRY SHAPE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. A flexipage booleanFilter has no
         honoured OR - this repo MEASURED that a parenthesised OR ('1 AND 2 AND (3 OR 4)') deploys,
         survives a retrieve and is then IGNORED BY THE RENDERER - so an "IN (Approved, Not Sent)"
         test has to be two entries. NDA_Record_Page introduced that shape and already carries two
         Advance_Stage entries; see its header. The two entries here are STRICTLY SAFER than that
         precedent: Status__c holds one value at a time, so they are mutually exclusive by
         construction and the button can never render twice.

         ⚠ THE 'Not Sent' ENTRY IS DEFENSIVE PARITY WITH THE SERVICE MAP, NOT A LIVE PATH. The
         user removed 'Not Sent' from Disposition_NDA in Setup on 2026-08-25 and a live aggregate
         that day measured ZERO rows carrying it, on either record type. It is unreachable from any
         picker and, because NDA__c.Status__c is a RESTRICTED value set whose record-type subset
         DML does enforce, unwritable by Apex, Flow or the API. It exists here because
         RecordStageAdvanceService still maps the hop on purpose ("do not prune them as dead
         code"), and a button that is missing where the server would have advanced the record is
         the harder defect to find. Delete this entry only when that map entry goes.

         =====================================================================================
         🔴 RETRACTED 2026-08-31 (TRANCHE 3 METADATA-FIX PASS, S-5) - ACQUISITION_NDA NO LONGER
         HAS A 'Sent' VALUE AT ALL. THE CONCLUSION BELOW STILL HOLDS FOR A DIFFERENT REASON.
         =====================================================================================
         The superseded sentence is quoted and retracted rather than deleted:

             RETRACTED: "ACQUISITION IS UNTOUCHED. 'Sent' is the acquisition NDA's TERMINAL stage
             (Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent), which is why the page rule pins record type
             as well as status: without it this button would offer to re-send an acquisition NDA
             that is already at 'Signed'."

         WHAT IS TRUE NOW: on 2026-08-27, BEFORE this file's own note above was written, the user
         removed 'Sent' from Acquisition_NDA's picklist subset entirely (see that record type's
         own 2026-08-27 amendment in
         `objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml`, written after a live
         `INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST` incident on this exact restricted field).
         Acquisition_NDA's live sequence is now THREE values, Pending -> Received -> Signed, with
         'Signed' terminal - not four, and 'Sent' is not a value that field can hold for that
         record type at all, in any position. `RecordStageAdvanceService.cls` (~line 1708) already
         reflects this correctly.

         THE CONCLUSION THIS PARAGRAPH EXISTED TO SUPPORT IS UNCHANGED, FOR A STRICTER REASON: the
         page rule pinning record type is still REQUIRED, but not merely to stop this button from
         "re-sending" an acquisition NDA already at its terminal - a restricted picklist's
         record-type subset is enforced by Apex DML (measured, see the record type file's own
         2026-08-20 correction), so writing 'Sent' onto an Acquisition_NDA row would now THROW
         `INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST` rather than silently re-advancing a completed
         record. The record-type pin is load-bearing either way; only the mechanism changed. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Sent</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
